# Line endings are normalised to LF in the index and on checkout, on every platform.
#
# The repo carries a lot of *generated but committed* text — CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md, subject_grants.toml,
# .drift/acks/*.toml, .test_durations, tests/data/errors/error_identity.txt, docs/errors/*.md, the migration
# goldens, the gateway model references — and each is produced by a writer that does not pass an explicit
# `newline` argument, so on Windows Python translates every "\n" to CRLF and the whole set churns in version
# control with no change of content. The gates would not notice: they all compare with universal-newline
# reads, which fold CRLF back to LF before the comparison. This file closes that class for tracked files
# regardless of which writer produced them; see wip/line-endings-writer-sweep.md for the writer-by-writer
# half, which is the structural fix and is tracked separately.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git to detect text from binary, so images and other binaries are untouched. No tracked
# file contained CRLF when this landed, so it introduces no renormalisation diff — it pins the invariant.
* text=auto eol=lf
